*
* START-HISTORY:
* 10 Nov 26 Windows port - from Linux 944d6ed3, d049d8bb, 1c127f7c (S.102 stages 1, 4 and 5), 87659a06 (S.176), c792b4a2 (S.179), e8c72d31 (S.185),
*              ad4a2cf6 and c1aca2a8 (S.186), carry area 14.  The code is Linux's; the words are Windows': a job is a Task Scheduler task registered by the
*              job helper (sd-jobs.ps1, through SET.JOB) and run as the Windows account SDSYS, an account's command is run by a task of its own Windows
*              account, and a damaged file is removed by an administrator from C:\ProgramData\SD\sd-jobs.  Messages 14045 and 11821 are 15045 and 12826.
*              The help record points at the Administrator page 17-scheduled-jobs.
* 2 Nov 26 dm  S.102 stage 5 (the docs review): a damaged file whose name is not a job name is said to be removed by root by hand (rm /etc/sdcore/jobs.d/<file>);
*              the page used to advise set.job delete, which refuses such a name.  The help record now points at the Administrator page 23-scheduled-jobs.
* 2 Nov 26 dm  New (S.102 stage 1, account jobs only: the batch gate's list; the schedules themselves are a later stage).  Made from tool_viewers.
* 2 Nov 26 dm  S.102 stage 4, the administrator's half: a second view, Jobs (J; A goes back), lists the jobs the root helper holds with their next and last runs,
*              and N, C, D and R make, change, delete and start one through SET.JOB, each after a box that shows the whole sentence and the schedule in words.
*              The page still writes nothing itself; SET.JOB asks the root helper (sd-elevate job-set | job-delete | job-run).
* 2 Nov 26 dm  The review: C refuses a damaged file whose name is not a job name before the form (the form could never be sent), as D and R do; the Command menu's
*              "Allow or stop allowing" belongs to the account view's panes only and is dim in the Jobs view, where Enter is C.
* 8 Nov 26 dm  S.176: F6 / Shift-F6 are the box keys of every page ($tk_aipage 'ring', the AI line one of the stops); Tab and Shift-Tab no longer switch the boxes
*              (Left and Right still do).  AI > Ask the AI is a menu entry of its own.
* 8 Nov 26 dm  S.179: Ctrl-T the theme (View > Theme) and Ctrl-K the keys of the page (Help > Keys), through $tk_std as on every page.
* 9 Nov 26 dm  S.185: an account's allowed commands are tested with LOCATE in lst<1,1>, the values; in <1> LOCATE walks the fields, so every command after the
*              first showed as not allowed and Enter offered to add it again.
* 9 Nov 26 dm  S.186: View > Mouse, the same on every page (the case act:std.mouse in both panes' handlers, through $tk_std).
* 9 Nov 26 dm  S.186: '/' finds a row by typing in either view ($tk_findrow; the owner: "Letters stay, '/' finds").
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   TOOL.JOBS
*
*   For the administrator only (it is refused, before anything is read, for anyone else; it is in SDSYS's VOC only).  A full-screen page, in the toolkit's frame
*   (140 columns by 43 lines at least), in two views.
*
*   ACCOUNT COMMANDS (the view it opens in; A comes back to it): the batch gate.  A session started with a command on the command line (sd COMMAND, which is how
*   a Task Scheduler task of an account's own Windows account runs SD) is refused unless the command is on the account's list in @SDSYS/batch.jobs.
*
*     Accounts   every registered account but SDSYS, with how many commands it may run that way
*     Commands   the paragraphs and sentences of the selected account's VOC (the only kinds the gate lets run), each allowed or not, and any listed name that is
*                no longer one
*
*   JOBS (J): the administrator's scheduled jobs, each a Task Scheduler task only an administrator can register that runs one of two fixed commands as the
*   administrator: its name, its schedule, its command, when it runs next and how its last run ended (SET.JOB's list, which asks the job helper and Task
*   Scheduler).  N makes a job, C changes the
*   selected one's command or schedule, D deletes it (its name is typed in the box) and R starts it now.  A damaged definition is shown so; it can be changed or
*   deleted, not started.
*
*   Keys: Up and Down move in the box, PgUp and PgDn move a page, Tab changes box, Enter or the space bar in Commands allows the command under the cursor or stops
*   allowing it (in Accounts it moves to Commands; in Jobs it is C), F5 reads the lists again, F1 or ? or a click on a [?] explains the box, Ctrl-Q leaves.  Esc or
*   F10 (or a click on the top row) opens the menu bar - File: Quit; Command: Allow or stop allowing; Job: New, Change, Delete, Run now; View: Jobs, Account
*   commands, Switch box, Refresh, Output; Help - and Alt and a title's letter opens that menu.  Ctrl-O (View > Output) shows or puts away the OUTPUT PANE: what
*   each command answered, newest first, for as long as the page is open.
*
*   THE PAGE WRITES NOTHING ITSELF.  Every change is SET.BATCH add | remove account command or SET.JOB add | change | delete | run name ..., shown with its effect in
*   a box answered Run or Cancel (Cancel is what Enter chooses) and run by $tk_run.  A name that holds a character $tk_run does not pass (anything but a-z, 0-9,
*   dot, dash and underscore) is shown with the command to type at the prompt.  A job's time is sent as hh.mm (SET.JOB reads it as hh:mm): $tk_run passes no colon.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
program $tool_jobs
$catalog $tool_jobs

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h
$include err.h
$include sl.h
$include tk.h

   prompt ''

   allow = 'set.batch set.job'                                   ;* the two commands this page may run
   PLAIN = 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789._-'             ;* the characters $tk_run lets through in a word
   JOBIDS = 'backup-all' : @fm : 'update-accounts'                ;* the job helper's job ids (sd-jobs.ps1)
   JOBCMDS = 'backup.account all' : @fm : 'update.accounts all'
   DAYS = 'mon' : @fm : 'tue' : @fm : 'wed' : @fm : 'thu' : @fm : 'fri' : @fm : 'sat' : @fm : 'sun'

   call $tk_open('tool.jobs', 'admin', ctx, err)
   if err # '' then
      display err
      stop
   end
   void kernel(K$AUDIT, 'tool start app=tool.jobs')

   keys = ''
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f1', 'help', 'help', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'enter', 'change', 'change', 'Accounts' : @sm : 'Commands', 1)   ;* the Jobs view's Enter is its own (C); the menu entry is dim there
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f6', 'box', 'pane', '', 1)                 ;* S.176: F6 / Shift-F6 move between the boxes on every page (Tab does not)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'j', 'jobs', 'jobs', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'a', 'account commands', 'accounts', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'n', 'new job', 'jnew', 'Jobs', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'c', 'change job', 'jchange', 'Jobs', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'd', 'delete job', 'jdelete', 'Jobs', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'r', 'run now', 'jrun', 'Jobs', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, '/', 'find', 'find', '', 1)                  ;* 9 Nov 26 (S.186): '/' finds a row by typing (letters are this page's commands)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f5', 'refresh', 'refresh', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'ctrl-q', 'quit', 'quit', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'ctrl-o', 'output', 'output', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'esc', 'menu', 'menu', '', 1)                ;* Esc closes the output pane when it is open, else opens the menu bar
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'quit', '&File', '&Quit', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'change', '&Command', '&Allow or stop allowing', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'jnew', '&Job', '&New job', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'jchange', '&Job', '&Change the job', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'jdelete', '&Job', '&Delete the job', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'jrun', '&Job', '&Run the job now', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'jobs', '&View', '&Jobs', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'accounts', '&View', '&Account commands', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'pane', '&View', '&Switch box', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'refresh', '&View', '&Refresh', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'find', '&View', '&Find a row', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'output', '&View', '&Output', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'help', '&Help', '&Help on this box', '', '')
   call $tk_std('keys', ctx, keys, '', '')                ;* S.179: Ctrl-T theme, Ctrl-K keys and their View and Help entries, as on every page
   * The AI line: offered only the pane switch, the output pane and refresh (allowing a command and every job action are NOT offered); a proposal is carried
   * out by the page's own key.
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'pane', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'output', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'refresh', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_aipage('init', ctx, keys, '', '', aout)

   pnames = 'Accounts' : @fm : 'Commands' : @fm : 'Jobs'

   VIS = 10                                                      ;* rows in a list (the list pane's height less 4: set by get.rects)
   JVIS = 16                                                     ;* rows in the Jobs box (set by get.rects)
   view = 1                                                      ;* 1 account commands, 2 jobs
   pane = 1
   ai = 1 ; atop = 1                                             ;* the row selected in Accounts, and the first row shown
   ci = 1 ; ctop = 1                                             ;* the same in Commands
   find.last = ''                                                ;* 9 Nov 26 (S.186): the text '/' asked for last
   ji = 1 ; jtop = 1                                             ;* the same in Jobs
   an = 0 ; anm = '' ; cn = 0 ; cnm = ''                         ;* read.all reads both before it fills them (BASIC does not short-circuit)
   jn = 0 ; jnm = '' ; jsch = '' ; jcmd = '' ; jid = '' ; jnext = '' ; jlast = '' ; jbad = '' ; jerr = ''
   jread = 0                                                     ;* 1 once the jobs have been read (they are read when the view is first shown)
   gen = 0
   msg = ''
   done = 0
   outopen = 0                                                   ;* 1 while the output pane is shown

   perr = ''
   gosub declare.layout
   gosub read.all
   gosub draw.all

   loop
      call $tk_menubar('draw', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, '', '', mr)
      call $tk_frame(ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, msg)
      call $sl_curat(0, ctx<TK.C.YSTAT>)
      nm = ''
      screen key returning nm
      mr = ''
      ao = ''
      if nm # '' then call $tk_aipage('key', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, nm, ao)
      if ao<1> = 'replay' then nm = ao<2>
      if ao<1> # '' then msg = ao<4>
      if nm # '' and ao<1> = '' then call $tk_menubar('key', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, nm, outopen, mr)
      if mr<1> # '' then nm = mr<4>
      begin case
         case ao<1> = 'taken'
            if ao<3> then
               gen += 1
               ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
               gosub draw.all
            end
         case nm = ''
            if status() = ER$EOF then exit
         case nm = 'guardquit'
            exit
         case nm = 'resize'
            call $tk_layout('refresh', ctx, '', chg)
            gosub get.rects
            gen += 1
            ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
            gosub draw.all
         case nm = 'mouse'
            gosub on.mouse
         case 1
            gosub on.key
      end case
      if done then exit
   repeat

   call $tk_close(ctx)
   stop

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- what the system says

* Every registered account but SDSYS by name, each with its path and its list; then the selected account's commands.  The selection is kept by name through a
* refresh.
read.all:
   old.acct = (if ai >= 1 and ai <= an then anm<ai> else '')
   names = ''
   apath = ''
   openpath @sdsys:@ds:'accounts' to acc.f then
      select acc.f to 9
      loop
         readnext id from 9 else exit
         if id # 'sdsys' then
            read arec from acc.f, id then
               locate id in names<1> by 'AL' setting lp else
                  ins id before names<lp>
                  ins arec<1> before apath<lp>
               end
            end
         end
      repeat
      close acc.f
   end
   an = dcount(names, @fm)
   anm = names
   alist = ''
   openpath @sdsys:@ds:'batch.jobs' to batch.f then
      for i = 1 to an
         read brec from batch.f, anm<i> else brec = ''
         lst = change(brec, @vm, @fm)
         keep = ''
         for j = 1 to dcount(lst, @fm)
            w = downcase(trim(lst<j>))
            if w # '' then
               locate w in keep<1> setting kp else keep<-1> = w
            end
         next j
         alist<i> = change(keep, @fm, @vm)
      next i
      close batch.f
   end
   ai = 1
   if old.acct # '' then
      locate old.acct in anm<1> setting op then ai = op
   end
   if ai > an then ai = an
   if ai < 1 then ai = 1
   gosub read.commands
   return

* The selected account's paragraphs and sentences (field 1 starting PA or S, the login's own test), in name order, and the names on its list that are not one:
* cnm, ctype ('PA', 'S' or '' for a listed name with no such VOC record), con (1 allowed)
read.commands:
   old.cmd = (if ci >= 1 and ci <= cn then cnm<ci> else '')
   cnm = '' ; ctype = '' ; con = ''
   cn = 0
   if an > 0 then
      openpath apath<ai>:@ds:'voc' to voc.f then
         select voc.f to 9
         loop
            readnext id from 9 else exit
            read vrec from voc.f, id then
               vt = upcase(trim(vrec<1>))
               t = ''
               if vt[1, 2] = 'PA' then t = 'PA'
               if vt[1, 1] = 'S' then t = 'S'
               if t # '' then
                  locate downcase(id) in cnm<1> by 'AL' setting lp else
                     ins downcase(id) before cnm<lp>
                     ins t before ctype<lp>
                  end
               end
            end
         repeat
         close voc.f
      end
      lst = alist<ai>
      for j = 1 to dcount(lst, @vm)
         locate lst<1, j> in cnm<1> by 'AL' setting lp else
            ins lst<1, j> before cnm<lp>
            ins '' before ctype<lp>
         end
      next j
      cn = dcount(cnm, @fm)
      for j = 1 to cn
         locate cnm<j> in lst<1,1> setting kp then con<j> = 1 else con<j> = 0      ;* <1,1>: lst is the values of one field (in <1> LOCATE walks fields, S.185)
      next j
   end
   ci = 1
   if old.cmd # '' then
      locate old.cmd in cnm<1> setting op then ci = op
   end
   if ci > cn then ci = cn
   if ci < 1 then ci = 1
   gosub keep.tops
   return

* The administrator's jobs, as SET.JOB lists them (it asks the job helper and Task Scheduler; the page reads nothing of theirs itself).  Lines:
*   job NAME: SCHEDULE: COMMAND (ID)          followed by   next run: X; last run: Y
*   damaged NAME: REASON
* The selection is kept by name.  jerr is what the verb said when the list could not be read.
read.jobs:
   old.job = (if ji >= 1 and ji <= jn then jnm<ji> else '')
   jnm = '' ; jsch = '' ; jcmd = '' ; jid = '' ; jnext = '' ; jlast = '' ; jbad = '' ; jerr = ''
   jn = 0
   jread = 1
   call $tk_run(allow, 'set.job', jout, jst, jrerr)
   jout = change(change(jout, char(13) : char(10), @fm), char(13), '')
   if jrerr # '' then
      jerr = jrerr
   end else
      if jst # 0 then jerr = trim(change(jout, @fm, '  '))
   end
   if jerr = '' then
      for i = 1 to dcount(jout, @fm)
         ln = jout<i>
         tl = trim(ln)
         begin case
            case ln[1, 4] = 'job '
               rest = ln[5, len(ln)]
               p = index(rest, ': ', 1)                          ;* the name ends at the first ': '; a schedule holds hh:mm, never ': '
               if p > 0 then
                  jn += 1
                  jnm<jn> = rest[1, p - 1]
                  rest = rest[p + 2, len(rest)]
                  p = index(rest, ': ', 1)
                  jsch<jn> = (if p > 0 then rest[1, p - 1] else rest)
                  rest = (if p > 0 then rest[p + 2, len(rest)] else '')
                  jcmd<jn> = trim(field(rest, '(', 1))
                  jid<jn> = field(field(rest, '(', 2), ')', 1)
                  jbad<jn> = ''
                  jnext<jn> = '' ; jlast<jn> = ''
               end
            case ln[1, 8] = 'damaged '
               rest = ln[9, len(ln)]
               p = index(rest, ': ', 1)
               if p > 0 then
                  jn += 1
                  jnm<jn> = rest[1, p - 1]
                  jbad<jn> = rest[p + 2, len(rest)]
                  jsch<jn> = '' ; jcmd<jn> = '' ; jid<jn> = '' ; jnext<jn> = '' ; jlast<jn> = ''
               end
            case tl[1, 10] = 'next run: ' and jn > 0
               t = tl[11, len(tl)]
               p = index(t, '; last run: ', 1)
               if p > 0 then
                  jnext<jn> = t[1, p - 1]
                  jlast<jn> = t[p + 12, len(t)]
               end
         end case
      next i
   end
   ji = 1
   if old.job # '' then
      locate old.job in jnm<1> setting op then ji = op
   end
   if ji > jn then ji = jn
   if ji < 1 then ji = 1
   gosub keep.tops
   return

* The first row shown in each box follows the selection
keep.tops:
   if ai < atop then atop = ai
   if ai > atop + VIS - 1 then atop = ai - VIS + 1
   if atop < 1 then atop = 1
   if ci < ctop then ctop = ci
   if ci > ctop + VIS - 1 then ctop = ci - VIS + 1
   if ctop < 1 then ctop = 1
   if ji < jtop then jtop = ji
   if ji > jtop + JVIS - 1 then jtop = ji - JVIS + 1
   if jtop < 1 then jtop = 1
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- drawing

* The layout: the two lists side by side in the first band, the explanation in the second and the help in the third, at 140 by 43 the sizes the retired tool.viewers had.
* Out: a.x a.y a.w a.h (Accounts), c.x c.y c.w c.h (Commands), m.x m.y m.w m.h (What this means), h.x h.y h.w h.h (Help), VIS.  The Jobs view has its own
* (jobs.layout), with one box the focus can be in.
declare.layout:
   if view = 2 then
      gosub jobs.layout
      gosub get.rects
      return
   end
   d = ''
   d<1> = 'accounts' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 14 : @vm : 50 : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   d<2> = 'commands' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 2 : @vm : 14 : @vm : 87 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   d<3> = 'means' : @vm : 2 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 17 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   d<4> = 'help' : @vm : 3 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 5 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   ctx<TK.C.FOCI> = 'accounts' : @sm : 'Accounts' : @vm : 'commands' : @sm : 'Commands'   ;* the boxes that take the focus, for $tk_frame's [*] / [-]
   call $tk_layout('declare', ctx, d, perr)
   if outopen then gosub open.layout
   gosub get.rects
   return

* With the output pane open: the same panes, the explanation 6 rows shorter and the output pane, 6 rows, between it and the help
open.layout:
   o = ''
   o<1> = 'accounts' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 14 : @vm : 50 : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   o<2> = 'commands' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 2 : @vm : 14 : @vm : 87 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   o<3> = 'means' : @vm : 2 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 11 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   o<4> = 'output' : @vm : 3 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 6 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   o<5> = 'help' : @vm : 4 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 5 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   call $tk_layout('declare', ctx, o, perr)
   return

* The Jobs view: the jobs across the body, the explanation and the help under them; with the output pane open the explanation gives it 6 rows.  One box takes
* the focus, so no marks.
jobs.layout:
   ctx<TK.C.FOCI> = ''
   d = ''
   d<1> = 'jobs' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 20 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   if outopen then
      d<2> = 'means' : @vm : 2 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 5 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
      d<3> = 'output' : @vm : 3 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 6 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
      d<4> = 'help' : @vm : 4 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 5 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   end else
      d<2> = 'means' : @vm : 2 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 11 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
      d<3> = 'help' : @vm : 3 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 5 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   end
   call $tk_layout('declare', ctx, d, perr)
   return

toggle.out:
   call $tk_out('toggle', ctx, '', '', oc)
   outopen = oc
   gosub declare.layout
   gen += 1
   ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
   gosub draw.all
   return

* The other view: its layout, its box with the focus, its lists (the jobs are read the first time they are shown)
switch.view:
   view = (if view = 1 then 2 else 1)
   pane = (if view = 2 then 3 else 1)
   gosub declare.layout
   if view = 2 and not(jread) then gosub read.jobs
   gen += 1
   ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
   gosub draw.all
   return

get.rects:
   call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, 'means', rc)
   m.x = rc<1, 1> ; m.y = rc<1, 2> ; m.w = rc<1, 3> ; m.h = rc<1, 4>
   call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, 'help', rc)
   h.x = rc<1, 1> ; h.y = rc<1, 2> ; h.w = rc<1, 3> ; h.h = rc<1, 4>
   m.tw = m.w - 4
   h.tw = h.w - 4
   if view = 2 then
      call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, 'jobs', rc)
      j.x = rc<1, 1> ; j.y = rc<1, 2> ; j.w = rc<1, 3> ; j.h = rc<1, 4>
      JVIS = j.h - 4                                             ;* the header row, the rows, a blank row and the border
   end else
      call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, 'accounts', rc)
      a.x = rc<1, 1> ; a.y = rc<1, 2> ; a.w = rc<1, 3> ; a.h = rc<1, 4>
      call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, 'commands', rc)
      c.x = rc<1, 1> ; c.y = rc<1, 2> ; c.w = rc<1, 3> ; c.h = rc<1, 4>
      VIS = a.h - 4                                              ;* the header row, the rows, a blank row and the border
   end
   gosub keep.tops
   return

draw.all:
